  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed residential accommodation, which includes a large number of 1-bedroom flats, does not provide an appropriate range of unit sizes to meet housing need in the area, contrary to Policy SD1 (Quality of Life) and Policy H8 (Mix of Units) of the London Borough of Camden Unitary Development Plan 2006. \r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed new building, by virtue of the inappropriate detailed design of the front elevation would fail to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Charlotte Street Conservation Area contrary to Policy B1 (General Design Principles), B2 (design and layout of developments large enough to change their context) and B7 (Conservation Areas) of the London Borough of Camden Unitary Development Plan (2006). \r\n"
  ],
